        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Exactly right — and your reasoning names the mechanism: probability here comes from **how many** tiles of each shape are in the bag, not from the order they went in.\n\nDrawing one tile at random means every tile is equally likely to be the one you pull:\n\n- Round: 3 of 4 tiles → **3/4 (75%)**\n- Square: 1 of 4 tiles → **1/4 (25%)**\n\nOne nuance worth holding onto: the \"drop one square, *then* add three round\" sequence matters for nothing statistically. A bag doesn't remember order. If the tiles got jumbled in a bag, the order of insertion is irrelevant — only the counts are. (Order would only matter if you drew tiles one at a time *without* replacing them, which is a different experiment — and then you'd be far more likely to end up with round tiles overall too, since you're exhausting the bag.)\n\nSo: round is your best single guess, and it's a 3-to-1 edge over square.\n\nLet me let you push on that number to check you believe it:"
          },
          {
            "type": "toolCall",
            "id": "call_function_hj68jsvwuwfe_1",
            "name": "interactive_page",
            "arguments": {
              "title": "Tile draw probability explorer",
              "description": "An interactive explorer for drawing one tile at random from a bag. A slider sets how many round tiles are in the bag (there is always 1 square tile). Two readouts show the probability of drawing a round tile and of drawing a square tile, updating as the slider moves. A bar shows the two shares side by side. A simulation runs 1,000 random draws and reports how many of each shape actually came up, so the learner can compare the observed counts to the predicted probabilities.",
              "purpose": "explore",
              "html": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<title>Tile draw probability explorer</title>\n<style>\n  :root { color-scheme: light dark; }\n  * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n  body { margin: 0; padding: 4px 2px; font-family: var(--font-sans, system-ui, sans-serif); color: var(--foreground); background: transparent; }\n  .panel { background: var(--card); color: var(--card-foreground); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 14px 16px; margin-bottom: 12px; }\n  h1 { font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 0 0 4px; }\n  p.sub { margin: 0 0 14px; color: var(--muted-foreground); font-size: 0.86rem; }\n  .row { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }\n  label { font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 600; }\n  input[type=range] { flex: 1 1 180px; min-width: 150px; }\n  .val { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; font-weight: 700; min-width: 3.5rem; text-align: right; }\n  .readouts { display: flex; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: 14px 0; }\n  .ro { flex: 1 1 140px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 10px 12px; }\n  .ro .lbl { font-size: 0.76rem; color: var(--muted-foreground); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em; }\n  .ro .num { font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }\n  .bar { height: 30px; display: flex; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid var(--border); }\n  .bar > div { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 600; color: #fff; overflow: hidden; white-space: nowrap; }\n  .r { background: var(--chart-1); }\n  .s { background: var(--chart-2); }\n  .legend { display: flex; gap: 14px; font-size: 0.8rem; margin-top: 8px; color: var(--muted-foreground); }\n  .chip { display: inline-block; width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 2px; margin-right: 5px; vertical-align: middle; }\n  button { font: inherit; padding: 8px 14px; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border); background: var(--primary); color: var(--primary-foreground); cursor: pointer; }\n  button.sec { background: var(--secondary); color: var(--secondary-foreground); }\n  .out { margin-top: 12px; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.5; }\n  .out .line { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 10px; padding: 3px 0; border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--border); }\n  .out .line:last-child { border-bottom: none; }\n  .mono { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; font-weight: 600; }\n  .note { font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--muted-foreground); margin-top: 10px; }\n  .sr { position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; overflow: hidden; clip: rect(0 0 0 0); }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"panel\">\n  <h1>Bag of tiles: 1 square, some number of round</h1>\n  <p class=\"sub\">Move the slider, then run 1,000 draws to see whether the bag actually behaves the way the odds predict.</p>\n\n  <div class=\"row\">\n    <label for=\"rounds\">Round tiles in the bag</label>\n    <input id=\"rounds\" type=\"range\" min=\"1\" max=\"9\" step=\"1\" value=\"3\">\n    <span class=\"val\" id=\"roundsVal\">3</span>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"readouts\">\n    <div class=\"ro\"><div class=\"lbl\">P(draw round)</div><div class=\"num\" id=\"pRound\">75%</div></div>\n    <div class=\"ro\"><div class=\"lbl\">P(draw square)</div><div class=\"num\" id=\"pSq\">25%</div></div>\n    <div class=\"ro\"><div class=\"lbl\">Total tiles</div><div class=\"num\" id=\"pTot\">4</div></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"bar\" id=\"bar\">\n    <div class=\"r\" id=\"barR\" style=\"width:75%\">Round 75%</div>\n    <div class=\"s\" id=\"barS\" style=\"width:25%\">Square 25%</div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"legend\">\n    <span><span class=\"chip r\" style=\"background:var(--chart-1)\"></span>Round</span>\n    <span><span class=\"chip s\" style=\"background:var(--chart-2)\"></span>Square</span>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"panel\">\n  <div class=\"row\">\n    <button id=\"sim\">Run 1,000 draws</button>\n    <button id=\"share\" class=\"sec\">Share what I found</button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"out\" id=\"out\" aria-live=\"polite\">\n    <div class=\"line\"><span>No run yet.</span><span class=\"mono\" id=\"oHead\">—</span></div>\n  </div>\n  <p class=\"note\" id=\"note\">Prediction: the observed share of round draws should land close to the predicted percentage, not exactly on it.</p>\n</div>\n\n<script>\n(function () {\n  var slider = document.getElementById('rounds');\n  var roundsVal = document.getElementById('roundsVal');\n  var pRound = document.getElementById('pRound');\n  var pSq = document.getElementById('pSq');\n  var pTot = document.getElementById('pTot');\n  var barR = document.getElementById('barR');\n  var barS = document.getElementById('barS');\n  var out = document.getElementById('out');\n  var oHead = document.getElementById('oHead');\n  var note = document.getElementById('note');\n\n  function state() { return { rounds: parseInt(slider.value, 10) }; }\n  function probs() {\n    var r = state().rounds, t = r + 1;\n    return { r: r, t: t, pr: r / t, ps: 1 / t };\n  }\n  function render() {\n    var p = probs();\n    roundsVal.textContent = p.r;\n    pRound.textContent = (p.pr * 100).toFixed(1) + '%';\n    pSq.textContent = (p.ps * 100).toFixed(1) + '%';\n    pTot.textContent = p.t;\n    barR.style.width = (p.pr * 100) + '%';\n    barS.style.width = (p.ps * 100) + '%';\n    barR.textContent = p.pr > 0.15 ? 'Round ' + (p.pr * 100).toFixed(0) + '%' : '';\n    barS.textContent = p.ps > 0.15 ? 'Square ' + (p.ps * 100).toFixed(0) + '%' : '';\n    var s = keating.getState();\n    if (s && typeof s === 'object') { s.rounds = p.r; keating.setState(s); }\n  }\n  slider.addEventListener('input', render);\n\n  var last = null;\n  document.getElementById('sim').addEventListener('click', function () {\n    var p = probs();\n    var n = 1000, gotR = 0, gotS = 0;\n    for (var i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n      var idx = Math.floor(Math.random() * p.t);\n      if (idx < p.r) gotR++; else gotS++;\n    }\n    var obsR = gotR / n, obsS = gotS / n;\n    last = { rounds: p.r, total: p.t, predicted: p.pr, observed: obsR, counts: { round: gotR, square: gotS } };\n    out.innerHTML = '';\n    function line(a, b) {\n      var d = document.createElement('div');\n      d.className = 'line';\n      var l = document.createElement('span'); l.textContent = a;\n      var r = document.createElement('span'); r.className = 'mono'; r.textContent = b;\n      d.appendChild(l); d.appendChild(r); out.appendChild(d);\n    }\n    line('Round drawn', gotR + ' of ' + n + '  (' + (obsR * 100).toFixed(1) + '%)');\n    line('Square drawn', gotS + ' of ' + n + '  (' + (obsS * 100).toFixed(1) + '%)');\n    line('Predicted round share', (p.pr * 100).toFixed(1) + '%');\n    line('Gap (observed - predicted)', ((obsR - p.pr) * 100).toFixed(1) + ' points');\n    note.textContent = 'Run it again and watch the gap shrink or change sign. The odds describe the long run, not any single draw.';\n  });\n\n  document.getElementBy"
            }
          }
